1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,632
My paintings never just capture a face. They capture time, stealing the youth right off the canvas.

2
00:00:07,932 --> 00:00:16,164
Yesterday I painted old Mr. Vance with deep wrinkles. Today, he woke up looking exactly like the portrait.

3
00:00:16,464 --> 00:00:23,472
Everyone called it a miraculous curse. I called it a terrifying power I could finally use.

4
00:00:23,772 --> 00:00:32,124
I mixed vibrant crimsons and smooth golds, desperate to paint myself the flawless youth I always wanted.

5
00:00:32,424 --> 00:00:40,800
Every brushstroke felt lighter. Every painted curve smoothed away the harsh realities of my tiring life.

6
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:49,332
I added the final shining highlight to the cheekbones, stepping back to admire my absolute masterpiece.

7
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:57,360
The canvas glowed with radiant life. But a strange, sudden chill swept through the quiet studio room.

8
00:00:57,660 --> 00:01:04,908
I turned around to look in the heavy floor-length mirror, expecting to see my gorgeous new face.

9
00:01:05,208 --> 00:01:13,464
The mirror showed only an empty, blank canvas staring back at me with terrifying, hollow eyes.

10
00:01:13,764 --> 00:01:20,676
If beauty demands a sacrifice, whose face will be left completely blank on the canvas?
